# Marks: setting, jumping with ' and `, operators, and how marks follow edits.

=== ma sets a mark without moving the cursor
ref:    motion.txt *m*
quote:  "Set mark {a-zA-Z} at cursor position (does not move the cursor, this is not a motion command)."
given:
  one
  tw|o
  three
keys:   ma
expect:
  one
  tw|o
  three
marks:  a=2:2

=== 'a jumps to the first non-blank of the mark's line
ref:    motion.txt *mark-motions*
quote:  "With ' (single quote): The cursor is positioned on the first non-blank character in the line of the specified location and the motion is linewise."
given:
  one
    tw|o
  three
keys:   maG'a
expect:
  one
    |two
  three

=== `a jumps to the exact position of the mark
ref:    motion.txt *mark-motions*
quote:  "With ` (backtick): The cursor is positioned at the specified location and the motion is |exclusive|."
given:
  one
    tw|o
  three
keys:   maG`a
expect:
  one
    tw|o
  three

=== d'a deletes linewise from the cursor line to the mark line
ref:    motion.txt *:delmarks*
quote:  "For example: \"d't\" deletes the lines from the cursor position to mark 't'."
given:
  one
  t|wo
  three
  four
keys:   majjd'a
expect:
  o|ne
regs:   "" = "two\nthree\nfour\n"   "1 = "two\nthree\nfour\n"

=== d`a deletes exclusively up to the mark
ref:    motion.txt *mark-motions*
quote:  "With ` (backtick): The cursor is positioned at the specified location and the motion is |exclusive|."
given:  one |two three
keys:   ma$d`a
expect: one |e
regs:   "" = "two thre"   "- = "two thre"

=== y`a yanks charwise backwards and leaves the cursor at the start
ref:    motion.txt *mark-motions*
quote:  "With ` (backtick): The cursor is positioned at the specified location and the motion is |exclusive|."
given:  one |two three
keys:   mawy`a
expect: one |two three
regs:   "" = "two "   "0 = "two "

=== y'a yanks the lines between the cursor and the mark
ref:    motion.txt *mark-motions*
quote:  "the motion is linewise."
given:
  |one
  two
  three
keys:   majy'a
expect:
  |one
  two
  three
regs:   "0 = "one\ntwo\n"

=== 'a with an operator to a mark below the cursor
ref:    motion.txt *mark-motions*
quote:  "the motion is linewise."
given:
  one
  |two
  three
  four
keys:   jmakc'aX<Esc>
expect:
  one
  |X
  four

=== a mark moves down when a line is inserted above it
ref:    motion.txt *:delmarks*
quote:  "Lowercase marks 'a to 'z are remembered as long as the file remains in the buffer list."
given:
  one
  t|wo
keys:   maggOnew<Esc>
expect:
  ne|w
  one
  two
marks:  a=3:1

=== a mark moves up when a line above it is deleted
ref:    motion.txt *:delmarks*
quote:  "Lowercase marks 'a to 'z are remembered as long as the file remains in the buffer list."
given:
  one
  two
  thr|ee
keys:   maggdd
expect:
  tw|o
  three
marks:  a=2:3

=== deleting the line with a mark erases the mark
ref:    motion.txt *:delmarks*
quote:  "If you delete a line that contains a mark, that mark is erased."
given:
  one
  t|wo
  three
keys:   madd
expect:
  one
  t|hree
marks:  a=(unset)

=== jumping to an erased mark is an error
ref:    motion.txt *mark-motions*
given:
  one
  t|wo
  three
keys:   madd'a
expect:
  one
  t|hree
msg:    "E20: Mark not set"

=== jumping to a mark never set is an error
ref:    motion.txt *E20*
given:
  one
  t|wo
keys:   'q
expect:
  one
  t|wo
msg:    "E20: Mark not set"

=== undo restores a mark on a deleted line
ref:    motion.txt *:delmarks*
quote:  "Lowercase marks are restored when using undo and redo."
given:
  one
  t|wo
  three
keys:   maddu
expect:
  one
  t|wo
  three
marks:  a=2:1

=== a change in the mark's line keeps the mark's column
ref:    oracle nvim v0.11.7
given:  one tw|o
keys:   ma0x
expect: |ne two
marks:  a=1:6

=== mA sets an uppercase mark usable in the same buffer
ref:    motion.txt *'A*
quote:  "To the mark {A-Z0-9} in the file where it was set"
given:
  one
  t|wo
  three
keys:   mAG`A
expect:
  one
  t|wo
  three
marks:  A=2:1

=== an uppercase mark follows inserted lines
ref:    motion.txt *:delmarks*
quote:  "The line number of the mark remains correct, even if you insert/delete lines or edit another file for a moment."
given:
  one
  t|wo
keys:   mAggOnew<Esc>
expect:
  ne|w
  one
  two
marks:  A=3:1

=== an uppercase mark works with an operator in the current file
ref:    motion.txt *:delmarks*
quote:  "You can only use an uppercase mark with an operator if the mark is in the current file."
given:
  |one
  two
  three
keys:   jmBggd'B
expect:  |three

=== '' returns to the line before the latest jump
ref:    motion.txt *''*
quote:  "To the position before the latest jump, or where the last \"m'\" or \"m`\" command was given."
given:
  one
    tw|o
  three
keys:   G''
expect:
  one
    |two
  three

=== `` returns to the exact position before the latest jump
ref:    motion.txt *``*
quote:  "To the position before the latest jump"
given:
  one
    tw|o
  three
keys:   G``
expect:
  one
    tw|o
  three

=== `` twice goes back and forth
ref:    motion.txt *``*
quote:  "To the position before the latest jump"
given:
  o|ne
  two
  three
keys:   G````
expect:
  one
  two
  t|hree

=== m` sets the previous context mark
ref:    motion.txt *m`*
quote:  "Set the previous context mark.  This can be jumped to with the \"''\" or \"``\" command"
given:
  o|ne
  two
  three
keys:   m`jj
expect:
  one
  two
  t|hree
marks:  ''=1:1

=== a jump sets the ' mark
ref:    motion.txt *''*
quote:  "To the position before the latest jump"
given:
  o|ne
  two
  three
keys:   G
expect:
  one
  two
  t|hree
marks:  ''=1:1   `=1:1

=== `[ and `] after a yank
ref:    motion.txt *'[*
quote:  "To the first character of the previously changed, or yanked text."
given:  one |two three
keys:   yw
expect: one |two three
marks:  [=1:4   ]=1:7

=== `] goes to the end of yanked text
ref:    motion.txt *']*
quote:  "To the last character of the previously changed or yanked text."
given:  one |two three
keys:   ye`]
expect: one tw|o three

=== '[ and '] after a linewise put
ref:    motion.txt *']*
quote:  "After inserting several lines with the \"p\" command you want to jump to the lowest inserted line: \"p']\"."
given:
  |one
  two
  three
keys:   y2jGp']
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  one
  two
  |three
marks:  [=4:0   ]=6:4

=== `[ and `] after a delete are the same position
ref:    motion.txt *']*
quote:  "After deleting text, the start and end positions are the same, except when using blockwise Visual mode."
given:  one |two three
keys:   dw
expect: one |three
marks:  [=1:4   ]=1:4

=== `[ and `] around inserted text after a change
ref:    motion.txt *']*
quote:  "This also works for text that has been inserted."
given:  one |two three
keys:   cwnew<Esc>
expect: one ne|w three
marks:  [=1:4   ]=1:7

=== '. is at the last change
ref:    motion.txt *'.*
quote:  "To the position where the last change was made."
given:
  one
  t|wo
  three
keys:   xgg`.
expect:
  one
  t|o
  three
marks:  .=2:1

=== '. after an insert
ref:    motion.txt *'.*
quote:  "To the position where the last change was made."
given:  one |two
keys:   iX<Esc>0
expect: |one Xtwo
marks:  .=1:4

=== '^ is where insert mode stopped
ref:    motion.txt *'^*
quote:  "To the position where the cursor was the last time when Insert mode was stopped."
given:  one |two
keys:   inew<Esc>0
expect: |one newtwo
marks:  ^=1:7

=== gi inserts where insert mode stopped last time
ref:    insert.txt *gi*
quote:  "Insert text in the same position as where Insert mode was stopped last time in the current buffer."
given:  one |two
keys:   inew<Esc>0giX<Esc>
expect: one new|Xtwo

=== '< and '> after a visual selection
ref:    motion.txt *'<*
quote:  "To the first line or character of the last selected Visual area in the current buffer."
given:  one |two three
keys:   ve<Esc>0
expect: |one two three
marks:  <=1:4   >=1:6

=== ]` goes to the next lowercase mark
ref:    motion.txt *]`*
quote:  "[count] times to lowercase mark after the cursor."
given:  |one two three
keys:   wmawmb0]`
expect: one |two three

=== 2]` with a count
ref:    motion.txt *]`*
quote:  "[count] times to lowercase mark after the cursor."
given:  |one two three
keys:   wmawmb02]`
expect: one two |three

=== [' goes to the previous line with a lowercase mark
ref:    motion.txt *['*
quote:  "[count] times to previous line with a lowercase mark before the cursor, on the first non-blank character in the line."
given:
    o|ne
  two
  three
keys:   maG['
expect:
    |one
  two
  three

=== g`a jumps without setting the ' mark
ref:    motion.txt *g`a*
quote:  "Jump to the {mark}, but don't change the jumplist when jumping within the current buffer."
given:
  |one
  two
  three
keys:   Gmaggg`a
expect:
  one
  two
  |three
marks:  ''=3:0
